          title: "Introduction",
          description: "What XENO Corpus does, the four states a claim can be in, and what it does not do yet.",
          body: "## Introduction\n\nA project depends on facts that quietly stop being true: the version in a README, a licence field, the port a service listens on, a rule in `CLAUDE.md` that an AI agent is told to follow. XENO Corpus keeps each of those facts as a **tenet**: a claim bound to the check that can prove it false. Every time the check runs, Corpus appends a **verdict**.\n\n| State | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Held** | The last check ran and the claim was true |\n| **Lapsed** | The last check ran and the claim was false |\n| **Unknown** | The check has never run, could not finish, or its result is too old. Corpus never guesses here |\n| **Attested** | A person vouched for it; no automatic check exists. It expires on its own clock |\n\nThe corpus is plain files inside your project, under `.xeno/corpus/`, so it goes into git with the code. Verdicts are only ever appended, so you can always see when a claim stopped holding.\n\n## What you can do with it\n\n- **See what is false right now.** The [Shape canvas](/docs/corpus/shape) answers *False now* and *Unchecked* directly.\n- **Read your agent instructions with every claim marked.** The [Document view](/docs/corpus/document-view) shows which lines are checked and which are not.\n- **Keep AI agents honest.** [Connect an agent](/docs/corpus/connecting-agents) and it receives the current state of the project before it acts, including every claim that is false.\n- **Ask questions.** `Ctrl+K` searches claims and documents and answers plain questions from the recorded verdicts.\n- **Script it.** The [`corpus` command](/docs/corpus/command-line) does everything the app does, from a terminal or CI.\n\n## What it is not yet\n\n- **Windows x64 only.** No macOS or Linux build exists.\n- **One person, one PC.** Team features (notifications, invitations, public badges, pull-request checks, single sign-on) need hosted Corpus, which is not available yet. The app marks each one *Needs hosted Corpus*. See [Local and hosted](/docs/corpus/local-and-hosted).\n- **Checks are not sandboxed.** A check is a command that runs with your permissions. See [Checks](/docs/corpus/checks).\n\n## Next steps\n\n- [Install XENO Corpus](/docs/corpus/installation)\n- [Your first corpus in five minutes](/docs/corpus/quickstart)",
