          body: "## Search and ask\n\nPress `Ctrl+K`. One box searches **claims**, **documents**, **source code** and **commands**. Use the arrow keys and `Enter`; `Esc` closes it.\n\n## Ask a question\n\nEnd the query with `?`. The answer comes from the claims and verdicts already recorded. Nothing is run to answer it. Depending on the answer you get a button: **Create a tenet for this** when nothing covers the question, **Open evidence**, or **View the canvas as of that pulse**. When nothing is close in meaning, a warning says the results may not answer the question.\n\n## It learns from what you open\n\nWhen you open a document from a search, Corpus remembers it on this PC (in `.xeno/local/corpus/`, never committed). Later searches that mean something similar rank it higher; the list dims briefly while it re-ranks. Nothing about it leaves your machine.\n\n## Query syntax\n\nOn the command line, `corpus search \"QUERY\"` accepts `tag:#name`, `path:\"a b\"` and `file:name`; prefix any of them with `-` to exclude.",
