          body: "## The projection\n\nThe projection is the corpus written for an agent to read, within a token budget:\n\n1. **Project instructions**, carried word for word. Corpus does not rewrite your `CLAUDE.md`.\n2. **Rules**, word for word. A paraphrased rule would be a new rule nobody reviewed.\n3. **False claims.** These are **never cut** for space. If they alone exceed the budget, they are printed in full and the projection reports `BUDGET_OVERFLOW`.\n4. **Unknown claims**, then **claims that hold**, cut first when space runs out.\n\nSee it in the app under **Integrations → Projection**, with a budget slider from 1,000 to 8,000 tokens, or on the command line:\n\n```\ncorpus context --budget 4000\ncorpus context --budget 4000 --task \"upgrade the payment client\"\n```\n\n`context` only reads; it runs no checks. `corpus project --for claude-code --out CLAUDE.md` writes the projection to a file for agents that read files rather than hooks.",
