          body: "## Command reference\n\nRun `corpus <command> --help` for the full usage of any command. *Runs* means it executes check commands; *writes* means it changes files under `.xeno/corpus/`.\n\n## Set up\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `init [--dry-run]` | Create a corpus for this project: derive checks and run them (writes, runs) |\n| `scan [PATH]` | A read-only first look at a repository with no corpus: what it would check, without writing anything |\n| `chain` | Show which corpora apply here, from the organisation down |\n| `vault DIR` | Index an Obsidian vault or any folder of Markdown into its own corpus |\n| `notes tree\\|read\\|daily\\|tags\\|backlinks\\|graph\\|search` | Read the project's notes in place; `daily` creates today's note |\n| `adopt --for claude-code\\|cursor\\|codex [--write]` | Connect an agent; see [Connecting AI agents](/docs/corpus/connecting-agents) |\n| `agents on\\|off\\|status` | Let Claude Code's reads teach search (this PC only) |\n\n## Check\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `pulse [--tenet ID]` | Run checks and append verdicts (runs, writes) |\n| `verify [--base BRANCH] [--no-run]` | Re-check only the claims this branch's changes touch; writes nothing. See [Checking a branch](/docs/corpus/checking-a-branch) |\n| `schedule set\\|status\\|tick\\|daemon` | Run pulses on a schedule; see [Scheduled pulses](/docs/corpus/scheduled-pulses) |\n| `baseline show\\|drop` | The lapses accepted when the corpus was created |\n\n## Claims\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `tenet show ID` | One claim, its check and its latest verdict |\n| `tenet test\\|new …` | Test a draft, or test and save it; see [Writing a tenet](/docs/corpus/new-tenet) |\n| `tenet revise ID … --reason R` | Save a new version |\n| `tenet assign ID… --owner O` | Change owners |\n| `tenet attest ID` | Vouch for a human claim (`--revoke --reason R` withdraws it) |\n| `tenet supersede ID --by ID --reason R` | Retire a claim in favour of another; its history stays |\n| `false-alarm TENET --reason …` | Record that a lapse was wrong |\n| `comment TENET \"TEXT\"` | Add a comment beside a claim |\n| `autofix status\\|enable\\|disable\\|revert\\|pause\\|resume` | Safe automatic fixes for version claims |\n| `challenge open\\|close\\|list` | Dispute a claim; the owner is asked, the verdict is unchanged |\n| `remember \"TEXT\" [--check CMD --expect V]` | Keep an unverified note; with a check, it becomes a proposal |\n\n## Documents\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `doc add\\|list\\|show\\|sync\\|supersede\\|check` | Registered documents |\n| `ingest FILE.md…` | Read claims out of documents into proposals; nothing is run |\n| `proposal list\\|show\\|add\\|approve\\|reject` | Review proposals |\n| `drift [--all]`, `drift ack DOC --reason R` | Documents whose code references changed |\n| `links [DOC] [--broken]` | The wiki-link graph between documents |\n\n## Read and ask\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `search \"QUERY\"` | Claims, documents and code. `--kind doc\\|claim\\|code` narrows it |\n| `ask \"QUESTION\"` | Answer from recorded claims and verdicts |\n| `context --budget N` | The projection agents read |\n| `project --for claude-code\\|codex\\|cursor --out PATH` | Write the projection to a file |\n| `used --query TEXT --document ID` | Record that a search led to a document (this PC only) |\n| `embed` | Build the local search index (no key, no network after the first install) |\n| `index`, `symbols build\\|status\\|definition\\|references\\|search` | Code indexes for source search and go-to-definition |\n| `badge TENET` | An SVG badge of a claim's state |\n\n## Record and audit\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `audit [--limit N] [--actor NAME]` | Every recorded action, newest first |\n| `integrity` | Verify the hash chains of every append-only log |\n| `attest [--require local\\|shared\\|evidence]` | Report which verdicts carry an attestation |\n| `export [--format json\\|intoto] [--out FILE]` | A report of claims, verdict history and the audit trail |\n| `decide SUBJECT --action TEXT`, `decisions [--review]` | Record decisions and the claims they relied on |\n| `reference` | Resolve claims that point at another corpus |\n\n## Serve\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `serve [--read-only] [--port N]` | The app's interface in your browser, on this PC only. It prints a launch link that grants access; do not share it |\n| `mcp` | The read-only MCP server over stdio |",
