          body: "## Exit codes\n\nEvery command uses the same codes, so a script can tell *it ran and found something* apart from *it could not run*.\n\n| Code | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `0` | Ran; nothing to report |\n| `1` | Ran and found something: a **new** lapse (`pulse`), a claim this branch would break (`verify`), a broken chain (`integrity`), drift (`drift`), broken links (`links`), a dangling reference (`reference`), an unattested verdict (`attest`), a decision taken over a claim that does not hold (`decide`) |\n| `2` | Usage error: a missing or wrong argument |\n| `3` | No corpus here: no `.xeno/corpus/` was found from this folder |\n| `4` | `ask` found no claim that covers the question |\n| `5` | Ran, but at least one check could not run (**Unknown**). `pulse` reports this even when there is also a new lapse |\n| `6` | Did not run: XENO Corpus is not signed in on this PC, the account has no access, or it has not been confirmed online for 14 days. Only the `corpus` command installed from the app returns this |\n\n## pulse in CI\n\n`pulse` fails with `1` only for a **new** lapse: one the baseline did not accept and the previous pulse did not already report. A lapse that is still unfixed on the next pulse does not fail again; it stays visible in the app and in `corpus context`.",
