          body: "## Files on disk\n\n## In the project\n\nEverything about the project's knowledge lives in `.xeno/corpus/`. **Commit it with the code.** The app never commits for you.\n\n| Path | Holds |\n|---|---|\n| `tenets/authored.json`, `tenets/derived.json` | Claims you wrote, and claims `init` derived |\n| `verdicts/*.jsonl` | Every verdict, one log per claim, append-only |\n| `runs/runs.jsonl` | Every pulse |\n| `baseline.json` | Lapses accepted when the corpus was created |\n| `documents/` | Registered documents and their revisions |\n| `doctrine/` | Rules carried to agents word for word |\n| `proposals/` | Claims read from documents, waiting for review |\n| `audit/audit.jsonl` | Every recorded action |\n| `drift.json` | Code references in documents, and whether they changed |\n\nTwo other folders are **per machine and never committed**; each carries its own `.gitignore`:\n\n- `.xeno/local/corpus/`: what search learned from your use, and your agent-learning decision.\n- `.xeno/cache/corpus/`: search indexes Corpus can rebuild.\n\n## On this PC\n\n- The app's own folder (**Help → Show Logs**) holds `auth.log` (each sign-in step, without passwords, tokens or email), `errors.log` (what failed, scrubbed the same way) and the last project you opened.\n- While the app or `corpus serve` runs, a discovery file for agents sits in `%USERPROFILE%\\.xeno\\capability-servers\\corpus.json`. It is removed on exit.\n\n## The .xcorpus file\n\nA pointer to the project folder, nothing more. See [Opening projects](/docs/corpus/opening-a-project).",
