          body: "## Troubleshooting\n\n## Sign-in does not finish\n\nThe browser must reach xenosystem.ai and then return to the app on this PC. **Help → Show Logs** opens the folder with `auth.log`, which records each step of the last sign-in without any password, token or email. The browser hands back to the app through `127.0.0.1` on this PC, so software that blocks local connections can stop it.\n\n## The project does not open\n\n- **Ports in use.** The app serves the project on this PC at port 30625, or 30626 or 30627 if that one is taken. Close any `corpus serve` you started in a terminal and try again.\n- **The installed interface is damaged.** Reinstall from the product page; your projects are not touched.\n\n## A screen stops working\n\nThe affected part of the window says *This screen stopped working* with **Reload**. If the whole window fails, XENO Corpus offers **Reload** or **Quit**. Either way the error is written to `errors.log` (**Help → Show Logs**).\n\n## A check stays Unknown\n\nThe check never finished. Select it: the inspector shows the last error output. Run its command yourself in a terminal in the project folder; a missing tool or a wrong path is the usual cause. A check that takes longer than 2 minutes is stopped.\n\n## `corpus` is not recognised\n\nOpen a **new** terminal after **Help → Install 'corpus' Command…**; terminals that were already open keep the old PATH. In Git Bash the command is `corpus` as well.\n\n## `corpus` says to sign in (exit 6)\n\nThe command follows the app's sign-in. Open XENO Corpus, sign in, and run the command again. If you are signed in, the app may not have confirmed your account online for 14 days: start it while connected.\n\n## `corpus` says there is no corpus (exit 3)\n\nIt looks for `.xeno/corpus/` from the current folder upwards. `cd` into the project, or pass `--from C:\\path\\to\\project`.\n\n## An agent does not see the corpus\n\nRun `corpus adopt --for claude-code` (without `--write`) in the project: it shows what is configured and what is missing. Restart the agent session after `--write`.",
